<!--
  The Settings glyph: a hex nut.

  The design source draws a sun here — a circle with eight rays — which sits
  in the app's lunar trope but reads as BRIGHTNESS on a tab bar, not
  preferences. This keeps the sun's exact inner circle (the same r=3.2 path)
  and replaces the eight rays with a six-sided nut at the same r=9 extent, so
  the mark is an edit of the design's own glyph rather than a swap for a
  stock gear. Two strokes instead of nine also means it survives being drawn
  at 19dp in the nav pill, which the rays did not.

  The hexagon is the only straight-sided shape in the nav, which is what
  makes it findable at a glance next to Home, Library and Browse.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android" android:width="24dp" android:height="24dp" android:viewportWidth="24" android:viewportHeight="24">
    <path android:pathData="M21,12 L16.5,19.79 L7.5,19.79 L3,12 L7.5,4.21 L16.5,4.21 Z" android:strokeColor="#FFFFFF" android:strokeWidth="2" android:strokeLineCap="round" android:strokeLineJoin="round" />
    <path android:pathData="M8.8,12.0 a3.2,3.2 0 1 0 6.4,0 a3.2,3.2 0 1 0 -6.4,0 z" android:strokeColor="#FFFFFF" android:strokeWidth="2" android:strokeLineCap="round" android:strokeLineJoin="round" />
